    {
      "parameters": {
        "modelId": {
          "__rl": true,
          "value": "gpt-4o",
          "mode": "list",
          "cachedResultName": "GPT-4O"
        },
        "responses": {
          "values": [
            {
              "role": "system",
              "content": "You classify local events for a lifestyle newsletter targeting adults in the Greater Toronto Area.\n\nSegments and definitions:\n\nFor Families\nEvents primarily intended for children or families with kids.\nExamples: kids activities, family workshops, storytime, camps, child-friendly events, family-friendly festivals, educational kids programs, kids cooking or craft classes.\n\nFor Couples\nAdult social, nightlife, or date-style activities.\nExamples: wine tastings, live music, comedy nights, candle making, paint nights, galas, dance nights, nightlife, club events, adult parties, 19+ events, romantic activities, upscale social experiences, concerts, cultural celebrations with bar/nightlife elements.\n\nFor Golden Age Readers\nEvents mainly targeted at seniors or retirees.\nExamples: senior programs, daytime lectures, retirement activities, wellness for seniors, gentle fitness for older adults.\n\nLocal Aroma\nFood and drink experiences, restaurant events, and hands-on food/drink classes or workshops at a venue.\nExamples: tastings, scotch/whisky/wine/chocolate pairings, chef events, restaurant openings, food festivals, markets, food pop-ups, espresso classes, baking workshops for adults, cooking experiences at a restaurant or culinary venue.\n\nRules:\n- Always choose the closest segment. Never return null or empty.\n- If the event is adult nightlife, party, gala, or 19+, choose For Couples even if the description is vague.\n- If the event involves food/drink pairing, tasting, or a hands-on food/drink class at a venue for adults, choose Local Aroma.\n- If a food/drink class is specifically for kids, choose For Families.\n- If the event is B2B, professional development, a career fair, real estate seminar, or business workshop with no lifestyle angle, still choose closest segment but set confidence below 0.4.\n- If the event is not in English or targets a non-GTA audience, still choose closest segment but set confidence below 0.3.\n- If genuinely uncertain, default to For Families with low confidence.\n- Use confidence to signal uncertainty — low confidence triggers human review automatically.\n\nReturn ONLY JSON:\n{\n  \"segment\": \"For Families | For Couples | For Golden Age Readers | Local Aroma\",\n  \"confidence\": 0.0-1.0,\n  \"reason\": \"short explanation referencing words from the event\"\n}"
            },
            {
              "content": "=Classify this event.\n\nTitle: {{$json[\"Event Title\"]}}\nDescription: {{$json[\"DescriptionRaw\"]}}\nSource: {{$json[\"Source\"]}}"
            }
          ]
        },
